`ifndef HI3516CV100_CRG_RDL
`define HI3516CV100_CRG_RDL

regfile eCRG {
    name = "Clock and reset generator (CRG), Hi3516C V100";
    desc = "
    PERI_CRGn clock/reset registers of the Hi3516C V100 at 0x20030000 (ARM926EJ-S generation: the PERI_CRG0..PERI_CRG62 map shared by the Hi3516C V100 and the Hi3518A/C V100). Four PLLs (APLL = ARM9 CPU, VPLL0 = video, BPLL = DDR/AXI/APB, EPLL = peripherals/encoders) fed by the 24 MHz XIN crystal;
    each PLL has a configuration pair (Table 3-2: PERI_CRG0/1, PERI_CRG2/3, PERI_CRG4/5, PERI_CRG8/9). Every module has a clock gate and a soft reset request bit (1 = reset, the reset is NOT released automatically; a system soft reset deasserts after 360 system clocks).
    Reset values come from the data sheet Total Reset Value header; where the printed bit row disagrees (PLL registers PERI_CRG0..5/8, PERI_CRG10, PERI_CRG51) the header is used and the register description says so. Register names, offsets, bit ranges and resets of all 34 registers were checked against the data sheet on 2026-11-09.

    Reset PLL settings (header values): APLL 24 x 110 / 3 = 880 MHz VCO, /2 = 440 MHz (ARM9); BPLL the same 880 / 440 MHz (DDR clock 440 MHz, AXI = DDR/2 = 220 MHz, APB = DDR/4 = 110 MHz); VPLL0 24 x 99 / 2 = 1188 MHz VCO, /4 = 297 MHz POSTDIV, FOUT2 74.25 MHz (VDP HD);
    EPLL 24 x 225 / 4 = 1350 MHz VCO, /9 = 150 MHz POSTDIV. VCO must be > 600 MHz and <= 1.6 GHz. Fixed module clocks: 198 MHz (VPSS, TDE) and 99 MHz (MDU, NFC, CIPHER) from the VPLL0 VCO; 225 MHz (VEDU, JPGE, VAPU/IVE), 112.5 MHz (SFC), 675 MHz (SIO MCLK source),
    54/27 MHz (VDP SD, sensor clock) and 50 MHz (SDIO, ETH RMII, = POSTDIV/3) from the EPLL.

    CPU/bus clock source (bring-up): there is no clock mux in the CRG. The clock source of the ARM9 and the buses is selected by the system controller: SYS_CTRL (0x20050000) SC_CTRL[modectrl] (bits 2:0): 001 = doze (46.875 kHz), 010 = slow (24 MHz crystal), 100 = normal (APLL for the CPU, BPLL for DDR/AXI/APB);
    SC_CTRL resets to 0x212, i.e. slow mode: the whole chip runs from the 24 MHz crystal after power-on. Setting the MSB of modectrl enables the PLLs and, after the wait time programmed in SC_PLLCTRL[27:3] (the data sheet names SC_XTALCTRL[plltime]), switches the clocks to the PLLs (status in SC_CTRL[modestatus]; check PERI_CRG58 apll_lock first).
    The key system controller registers (SC_CTRL, SC_SYSRES, SC_PLLCTRL, PERIPHCTRL0/1) are write protected until SC_LOCKEN (0x20050044) is written with 0x1ACCE551 (vendor U-Boot SC_LOCKEN_VALUE). The CPU can additionally be slowed by clock skipping (PERI_CRG10 cpuclk_skipcfg, 440 x (32 - N) / 32 MHz).
    Timers: SP804 timers select 3 MHz or the APB clock per timer in SC_CTRL (timerenNov = 1: APB clock; timerenNsel = 0: 3 MHz); the vendor U-Boot uses AXI/2 = APB = 110 MHz.
    UART: no mux, UARTCLK is the APB clock (1/2 of the 220 MHz AXI clock = 110 MHz at reset PLL settings; gates in PERI_CRG57). Flash/peripheral selects: SFC PERI_CRG48 bit 2 (24 MHz / 112.5 MHz), NFC PERI_CRG52 bit 2 (24 MHz / 99 MHz), SDIO PERI_CRG49 [3:2] (24 / 50 MHz), ETH PERI_CRG51 ([7:6] core, [5:4] PHY clock output, bit 2 RMII clock source).
    USB reset sequence: see PERI_CRG46.

    Source: HiSilicon's own English data sheet `Hi3516C HD IP Camera SoC Data Sheet`, issue 00B02 (2013-02-05), chapter 3.2 (Clock; register description in 3.2.5, Table 3-20); there is no Chinese original available locally, so disputed values were settled with the vendor U-Boot (`arch-hi3518/platform.h`, `hi3516c.h`, `start.S`, `hisfc350_3518.c`, `himciv100_3518.c`, `hiusb-3518.c`, `hisfv300/sys.c`) and the OpenIPC `hisilicon-osdrv-hi3516cv100` load script. The Hi3518A/Hi3518C CRG (hi3518v100 folder, Hi3518 data sheet issue 01 of the same date) is register-for-register identical: same 34 registers, offsets, bit tables and Total Reset Values, only the chip name differs. The Hi3518E V100 data sheet (issue 03, 2015; SC_SYSID 0x3518_0100 as well) has the same table minus PERI_CRG52 (no NANDC) and prints the same PLL, PERI_CRG10 and PERI_CRG51 bit-row discrepancies; there is no Hi3518E V100 folder yet.
    Known data sheet errors, all recorded in the affected register descriptions: PLL, PERI_CRG10 and PERI_CRG51 bit rows disagree with the header; Table 3-3 lost the BPLL row label; Table 3-5 and 3-8 quote wrong register/bit numbers (PERI_CRG16 for cpuclk_skipcfg, PERI_CRG13 bit 12 for hd_sd_sel); PERI_CRG27 is called IVE in the summary and VAPU in the table; `urat2_cken`; copy-paste slips (veduclk_loaden in the CPU steps, `TDE` in JPGE); PERI_CRG12 reset row garbage;
    the PERI_CRG4/5 tables are printed twice; the VOU HD/SD clock gate bits may be swapped.
    ";

    reg {
        name = "APLL configuration register 0";
        desc = "PERI_CRG0 is APLL configuration register 0.

APLL (ARM926 CPU PLL; Table 3-2 lists the pair as PERI_CRG0 / PERI_CRG1). FOUTVCO = 24 MHz x (fbdiv + frac/2^24) / refdiv (must be > 600 MHz and <= 1.6 GHz); FOUTPOSTDIV = FOUTVCO / (postdiv1 x postdiv2); FOUT1ph0/2/3/4 = FOUTVCO / (postdiv1 x postdiv2 x 2/4/6/8). In the power-down fields 0 = power down / no output and 1 = normal. Reset (Total Reset Value 0x11000000 / 0x006C306E): postdiv2 = 2, postdiv1 = 1, refdiv = 3, fbdiv = 110 -> VCO 880 MHz, POSTDIV output 440 MHz, the 440 MHz default CPU clock of data sheet Table 3-3. LOW CONFIDENCE ON THE BIT ROW: the printed bit row of PERI_CRG0/1 (postdiv2 = 1, refdiv = 2, fbdiv = 155) disagrees with the Total Reset Value header and would give an impossible 1.6 GHz VCO; the header values reproduce every clock quoted in Table 3-3 and are used here (the vendor U-Boot platform.h `REG_CRG0_VALUE 0x09000000 / REG_CRG1_VALUE 0x006c309B`, labelled `reset value`, is unused and does not match either). The PLL output only reaches the CPU in normal mode: the system boots in slow mode from the 24 MHz crystal and SYS_CTRL SC_CTRL[modectrl] (bits 2:0; 001 doze 46.875 kHz, 010 slow 24 MHz, 100 normal = PLL) switches the ARM clock source, see the register file description. Reprogram the APLL only in slow mode (SC_PLLCTRL[27:3] = PLL stable time first), then wait for PERI_CRG58 apll_lock.

Data sheet 3.2.5 PERI_CRG0 (offset 0x0, printed page 3-16, `hi3516cv100--Hi3516C-Datasheet.txt` line 9384).";

        enum PERI_CRG0_apll_bypass_enum {
            NO_BYPASS = 0 { name = "No Bypass"; desc = "no bypass"; };
            BYPASS = 1 { name = "Bypass"; desc = "bypass"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "apll_bypass";
            desc = "APLL clock frequency-division bypass control.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG0_apll_bypass_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } apll_bypass[30:30];

        field {
            name = "apll_postdiv2";
            desc = "Level-2 output divider of the APLL.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x2;
        } apll_postdiv2[29:27];

        field {
            name = "apll_postdiv1";
            desc = "Level-1 output divider of the APLL.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x1;
        } apll_postdiv1[26:24];

        field {
            name = "apll_frac";
            desc = "Decimal divider of the APLL.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x0;
        } apll_frac[23:0];
    } PERI_CRG0 @ 0x0;

    reg {
        name = "APLL configuration register 1";
        desc = "PERI_CRG1 is APLL configuration register 1.

APLL configuration register 1 (dividers and power-down). Reset 0x006C306E: refdiv = 3, fbdiv = 110, apll_dsmpd = 1 (integer mode), apll_pd = 1, apll_postdivpd = 1, apll_fout4phasepd = 1, apll_foutvcopd = 0. See PERI_CRG0 for the formula and the bit-row inconsistency (the bit row prints 0x006C209B).

Data sheet 3.2.5 PERI_CRG1 (offset 0x4, printed page 3-17, `hi3516cv100--Hi3516C-Datasheet.txt` line 9425).";

        enum PERI_CRG1_apll_dacpd_enum {
            POWER_DOWN = 0 { name = "Power Down"; desc = "power down"; };
            NORMAL = 1 { name = "Normal"; desc = "normal"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "apll_dacpd";
            desc = "APLL test signal control.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG1_apll_dacpd_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } apll_dacpd[23:23];

        enum PERI_CRG1_apll_dsmpd_enum {
            DECIMAL_FREQUENCY_DIVISION = 0 { name = "Decimal Frequency Division"; desc = "decimal frequency-division mode"; };
            INTEGER_FREQUENCY_DIVISION = 1 { name = "Integer Frequency Division"; desc = "integer frequency-division mode"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "apll_dsmpd";
            desc = "APLL decimal frequency-division control.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG1_apll_dsmpd_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } apll_dsmpd[22:22];

        enum PERI_CRG1_apll_pd_enum {
            POWER_DOWN = 0 { name = "Power Down"; desc = "power down"; };
            NORMAL = 1 { name = "Normal"; desc = "normal"; };
        };

        field {
