    reg {
        name = "BPLL configuration register 0";
        desc = "PERI_CRG4 is BPLL configuration register 0.

BPLL (DDR/AXI/APB PLL). FOUTVCO = 24 MHz x (fbdiv + frac/2^24) / refdiv (must be > 600 MHz and <= 1.6 GHz); FOUTPOSTDIV = FOUTVCO / (postdiv1 x postdiv2); FOUT1ph0/2/3/4 = FOUTVCO / (postdiv1 x postdiv2 x 2/4/6/8). In the power-down fields 0 = power down / no output and 1 = normal. Reset (Total Reset Value 0x11000000 / 0x006C306E): the same numbers as the APLL: VCO 880 MHz, POSTDIV 440 MHz = DDR clock; AXI = DDR / 2 = 220 MHz; APB = DDR / 4 = 110 MHz (Table 3-3, whose row label for this PLL is lost in the data sheet: it prints a second `APLL` row; the vendor U-Boot get_bus_clk() reads PERI_CRG4/5 to compute busclk = VCO / (2 x postdiv1 x postdiv2) = 220 MHz, which confirms BPLL). The data sheet describes this register twice (a page-break copy); the copies agree. LOW CONFIDENCE ON THE BIT ROW (prints postdiv2 = 1, postdiv1 = 1); the header is used.

Data sheet 3.2.5 PERI_CRG4 (offset 0x10, printed page 3-19, `hi3516cv100--Hi3516C-Datasheet.txt` line 9568).";

