ARM9/DDR frequency mode and reset configuration. The bit-row label `freqmode_a9_sys` has no entry in the bit table. The CPU clock skip: cpuclk_skipcfg = N disables N beats out of every 32 CPU clocks; write cpuclk_skipcfg, then cpuclk_loaden 0 -> 1 (the data sheet lists `write 0, write 1`). Table 3-5 attributes cpuclk_skipcfg to `PERI_CRG16 bit[9:5]`; that is a slip for PERI_CRG10. LOW CONFIDENCE ON THE RESET: the Total Reset Value header is 0x00000010 (cpu_srst_req = 1, skipcfg = 0) while the bit row prints skipcfg = 1 (0x20); the header is used (no vendor code reads it back). cpu_srst_req is valid only in slave loading mode; in normal (master) boot the bit has no effect on the running CPU.

Data sheet 3.2.5 PERI_CRG10 (offset 0x28, printed page 3-23, `hi3516cv100--Hi3516C-Datasheet.txt` line 9809).";

