    reg {
        name = "USB clock and soft reset control register";
        desc = "PERI_CRG46 is a USB clock and soft reset control register.

USB 2.0 host (EHCI/OHCI) clock and reset. Reset 0xB7 (the printed bit row says 0xFF, i.e. bits 6 and 3 set too; the header matches the six listed fields, bits 6 and 3 are RW reserved and read 0 per the header): clock on, controller/hub/PHY/bus all in reset. Vendor U-Boot hiusb-3518.c bring-up order: (1) clear SYS_CTRL PERI1_USB (0x20050084, = PERIPHCTRL21) bit 22 usbphy_shutdown (the PHY is powered down by setting it, DS 3.10.4); (2) one write to PERI_CRG46 that sets usb_cken and clears usb_ctrl_utmi0_req, usb_ctrl_hub_req, usbphy_port0_treq, usbphy_req and usb_ahb_srst_req together; udelay(10); (3) SYS_CTRL PERI_USB (0x20050080, = PERIPHCTRL20): set ulpi_bypass_en (bit 3), clear wordinterface (bit 0), ss_burst16_en (bit 9) and usbovr_p_ctrl (bit 17); udelay(10). The OpenIPC script writes 0x000121A8 to PERI_USB. Bits 6 and 3 are RW reserved; the bit row also names usb_ctrl_utmi1_req / usbphy_port1_treq (port 1 does not exist on this chip).

Data sheet 3.2.5 PERI_CRG46 (offset 0xB8, printed page 3-37, `hi3516cv100--Hi3516C-Datasheet.txt` line 10594).";

        enum PERI_CRG46_usb_cken_enum {
            DISABLED = 0 { name = "Disabled"; desc = "disabled"; };
            ENABLED = 1 { name = "Enabled"; desc = "enabled"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "usb_cken";
            desc = "USB PHY reference clock gating.";
