    reg {
        name = "SDIO clock and soft reset control register";
        desc = "PERI_CRG49 is an SDIO clock and soft reset control register.

SDIO clock and soft reset. Reset 0x2. The vendor U-Boot himciv100_3518.c clears `SDIO0CLK_PCTRL (1 << 3)` and sets `SDIO0CLK_SEL_50M (1 << 2)`: the effective value is sdioclk_sel = 01 (50 MHz); the vendor macro name for bit 3 does not match this data sheet, where bit 3 is the upper bit of sdioclk_sel and the sampling-phase bit is bit 4. Bits [31:5] are RW reserved. OPEN ITEM: the data sheet contradicts itself on the bit positions. The bit table (used here) has sdioclk_pctrl = bit 4 and sdioclk_sel = bits [3:2] (00 = 24 MHz, 01 = 50 MHz, 1X reserved), but clock Table 3-16 (data sheet text) says `sdioclk_pctrl ... PERI_CRG49 bit[3]` and a 1-bit `sdioclk_sel ... PERI_CRG49 bit[2]` (0 = 24 MHz, 1 = 50 MHz), as do the vendor U-Boot and Linux drivers (SDIO0CLK_PCTRL = 1 << 3, SDIO0CLK_SEL_50M = 1 << 2). The older Hi3516 V100 CRG also has the sample phase at bit 3 of its SDIO0 field. The select encoding (bit 2 = 1 -> 50 MHz) is the same in both readings; only the location of the sample-phase bit (3 or 4) is unresolved, and the vendor drivers never set it.

Data sheet 3.2.5 PERI_CRG49 (offset 0xC4, printed page 3-39, `hi3516cv100--Hi3516C-Datasheet.txt` line 10693).";

